.TH OPENBGI 1 "2026" "OpenBGI 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
openbgi \- play the games of the BGI/Ethornell visual-novel engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B openbgi
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ GAME
.RI [ "the game's own arguments" ]]
.br
.B openbgi
.I COMMAND
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
OpenBGI is a reimplementation of Ethornell's Buriko General Interpreter.
.I GAME
is a game's folder, a zip archive or a disc image (.iso) of one, or a
file in its folder.
Without it the game of the current folder is played, and where there is
none the launcher is shown: a list of the games in the folders it was
told about.
.PP
Nothing of a game is changed when it is played from an archive, a disc
image or a folder that cannot be written to: what it saves goes to the
user's data folder.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-engine= NAME
The engine profile, instead of detecting the game
.RB ( \-\-list\-engines ).
.TP
.BI \-\-games= FILE
The
.I openbgi.json
to know the game by; it is used whatever it is.
.TP
.BI \-\-productname= NAME
The product name the game's scripts ask for.
.TP
.B \-\-overlay
Play a folder without writing into it.
.TP
.BI \-\-patch= FILE
Lay a zip archive or a folder of files over the game; may be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-\-lang=en | ja
The language of OpenBGI's own messages.
.TP
.B \-\-launcher=dialog
Without a game, ask with the system's dialog
.RB ( =program :
the launcher).
.TP
.B \-\-preview=none
The launcher makes no first pictures of games that were never played.
.TP
.BR \-\-dialogs=frame | host
Message boxes drawn in the game's picture, or as windows.
.TP
.BR \-\-movies=decoder | player
Movies by the built-in decoder, or by the system's player first.
.TP
.BR \-\-stand\-in\-font=gothic | mincho | auto
The built-in font that stands in for a missing one.
.TP
.BR \-\-own\-pad\-keys=on | off
Take or ignore the keys a game gives a pad's controls itself.
.TP
.BR \-\-child\-windows=frame | host
Child windows drawn in the game's picture (the default), or as windows
of their own.
.TP
.B \-\-disc\-marker
Let the scripts see the disc's marker file.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-disc\-check
The game counts as registered.
.TP
.BI \-\-enable= FAMILY:OP
Make an opcode available whatever the profile says
.RB ( \-\-disable=
removes one).
.TP
.BR \-\-debug [ =pause ]
Open the debugger with the game.
.TP
.B \-\-detect
Print how the game is identified, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-engines
Print the engine profiles, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-missing
Print the opcodes of the profile that have no handler, and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-list= ARCHIVE
Print the entries of an archive, and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-extract= ARCHIVE
Write the entries of an archive into a folder, and exit
.RB ( \-\-out=\fIDIR\fP ,
.BR \-\-entry=\fINAME\fP ,
.BR \-\-raw ,
.BR \-\-convert ).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the options and the commands, and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
The tools are commands of the same program;
.B openbgi help
.I COMMAND
prints a command's arguments.
.TP
.B dump
Every archive of a game into files to edit.
.TP
.B pack
The archives again, from a dump.
.TP
.B scn
Scenario files: decompile, compile, list.
.TP
.B asm
Programs as listings: disassemble, assemble.
.TP
.B bpc
Programs in the source language: decompile, compile.
.PP
A folder named like a command is given as
.IR ./NAME .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I openbgi.json
The engine profiles, the games OpenBGI knows and the launcher's
settings.
It is looked for in the game's folder, then beside the program, then in
the user's data folder, where a new one is made when there is none.
A file in one of those places that cannot be written is not used,
unless it says
.B "\(dqstaticConfig\(dq: true"
at its top: then it is used as it is and never written.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/openbgi/
The user's data folder
.RI ( ~/.local/share/openbgi/
by default): the settings, the launcher's pictures and icons, and what
the games that are played from archives write.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BGI_GAMES
The
.I openbgi.json
to use, as
.BR \-\-games= .
.TP
.B BGI_LANG
The language of the messages, as
.BR \-\-lang= .
.TP
.B BGI_ENGINE
The engine profile, as
.BR \-\-engine= .
.TP
.B BGI_DATA
Where the folders of the games that are played from archives go, in
place of the user's data folder.
.TP
.B BGI_DPI
The desktop's scale in dots per inch (96 is 100 %, 144 is 150 %), when
it is read wrongly.
.TP
.B BGI_GL
.B off
never shows the picture through OpenGL;
.B force
uses OpenGL even when software draws it.
.TP
.BR BGI_FONT_GOTHIC ", " BGI_FONT_MINCHO ", " BGI_FONT
A font file for the games' Gothic or Mincho text.
.SH SEE ALSO
The documents installed with the program, and https://openbgi.net.
